WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Red-Hot Daydream!</b>

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:07.940
Okay.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.610
Fried rice good to go!

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.360
Huh? You got a new phone?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.430
Yeah, it's the latest model. 
There's a new app I wanted to check out.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.630
You can look up flights 
across the world in real time.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.000
This stuff is just so much fun to watch.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.400
Huh...

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.300
Oh, my bad. You wouldn't find it very fun, 
what with your hate for tech.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.570
Yeah, yeah, I can't keep up with technology.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.930
People act like I'm a Luddite or something.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.160
Troglodyte or not, I'll always love ya.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.260
You jerk!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.110
But, you know, you might actually be lucky.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.240
Huh? What do you mean?

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.670
This might sound cliché,

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.500
but convenient tools, when misused, 
can turn into dangerous weapons.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.070
Mankind may create and own tech,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.650
but we can also end up 
being controlled by it.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.950
That's how it's always been.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:04.950
Eventually, progress itself 
might turn its back on us.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.640
I'm Natsume Akira.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.560
I used to be a perfectly ordinary high schooler 
until I got into an accident

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.310
and woke up sixteen years later 
as just a brain,

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.340
forced to fight battles 
I couldn't make heads nor tails of.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.820
But if I try my best, 
maybe I can go back to being human.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.200
Hoping against hope for that wish to come true, 
I continue to work with the police.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.340
What the heck is this?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.130
You're nothing but a brain.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.160
A weapon.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.340
No longer human.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.140
Shut up. Who are you, anyway?

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.120
Deep down, you already know.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.470
No...

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.720
<b>destroy</b>

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.720
Destroy...

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.010
Stop...

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.640
<b>destroy</b>

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.640
Destroy.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.140
Stop it!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.600
<b>destroy it all</b>

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.600
Destroy it all!

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:41.380
Wait, I have a body.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.540
Is this... my room?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.910
Huh?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.160
"2014"?

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.630
Isn't that when I got into an accident?

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.330
Was it all just a bad dream?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.630
<b>Natsume</b>

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.630
What's taking you so long?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.140
Minami?!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.180
Why aren't you ready yet?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.000
We'll be late for school.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.620
I came all the way to wake
you up, so hurry up.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.040
Huh? Uh...

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.380
O-Okay.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:15.770
You had a bad dream?

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.230
Yeah, and a real weird one, at that.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:20.140
What about?

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:25.780
Well, it was 2030, and you were a cop 
with an android partner.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.600
And I'd been reduced to just a brain.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:31.870
Ridiculous, right?

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:35.610
Man alive, am I ever glad that wasn't real.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.470
On your feet!

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:40.410
Bow!

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.090
Take your seats!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.400
Good morning, my dear students. 
Say hi to Iriya. She just transferred in.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.830
I'm Iriya Alma. Nice to meet you.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.780
Huh? Wasn't she the...

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:54.340
Take the seat next to Natsume over there.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.190
Got it.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.460
I can't stop thinking about that girl.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.270
Ow!

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:13.290
Damn it, Akira! Watch where you're going, man!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.520
Oh, hey, Kimura. Didn't see you there, sorry.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.160
Why, you little...

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.790
You tryin' to play down 
my overwhelming presence here?

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.990
Hey, you two punks!

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:25.360
You got some balls of steel 
to be fighting in <i>my</i> halls.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.320
How 'bout I soften 'em up for ya?

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.800
Yikes! It's Kondo, the school counselor!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.940
Run for it!

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:36.070
No running in the hallways! 
Get yer asses back here!

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.280
Sorry!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.340
A... ki... ra!

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.000
Ow!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:55.040
<b>Infirmary</b>

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.040
Wow, sounds like you had a rough time.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.100
But enjoy it while it lasts. 
Ah, to be young again.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.580
There. You're as good as new.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.420
Thank you very much.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.560
Hey, is there really a point to acting out 
this B-grade high-school anime?

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.140
This crap is nothing like real life.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.250
Of course it isn't.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.190
This is just a fantasy world.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.120
Let me out of here for a bit.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.780
You got it.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.500
Logging you out.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.470
These guys are such good sports. 
It's making me cry.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.120
How's it looking?

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.970
They're all enjoying 
a generic-ass school life in full VR.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.950
Chief, will this really awaken Akira's memories?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.280
I'm gonna be late!

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:02.890
Are you okay?

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.960
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:09.470
God <i>damn.</i> This guy's got one 
messed-up idea of teenage life.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.200
This world's been built 
from Akira's conscious.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.360
If we want to investigate his memories here,

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.330
we'll have to poke at the things 
he avoids or dislikes.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.220
Like what?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.060
Don't you notice anything off 
about the streets?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.900
There are hardly any vehicles 
operating in this world.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.670
Oh, yeah. Akira did get in
an accident, didn't he?

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.160
Also, nobody has a cellphone.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.700
That, too, is part of his desire. 
He hates technology, after all.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:50.170
So, you say we can awaken his memories 
by pushing those angles?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.960
That is my assumption, yes.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.540
And how do we do that, exactly?

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.450
What's the matter, Alma?

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.460
I've got an idea.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.880
His accident must be a huge source 
of trauma for him.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:08.070
Reenacting one in his presence 
should do the job.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:09.720
Got it.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.210
Hey, Akira.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.460
The truck...

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.640
disappeared?!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.130
Hey, don't space out 
in the middle of the street.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:30.090
You can be pretty absentminded, huh, Alma?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.240
Alma, what just happened?

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.210
That was unexpected. 
My AI failed to intervene.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.450
Well, I'm sure it was just a minor error,

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.170
but we should all log out just in case.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:00.930
Aw, I was having fun.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.880
Hmm? What's going on?

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.030
You can't be serious!

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.100
What's the matter?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.380
I can't access the system controls.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.810
I have no idea why, but it looks like 
we're not gonna be able to log out.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.760
Wait, you mean we're trapped 
here in this VR space?

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.850
Unfortunately, yes.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.740
Are you kidding me?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:30.200
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.480
Yeah, this is fun.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.720
But something's off.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.170
I get the feeling 
I'm forgetting something important.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.700
And what would that be?

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.660
Who are you, anyway?

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.420
I'm Ygg!

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.330
"Yggdrasil"?

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.290
Yeah.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:56.080
A quantum computer Iriya has in operation.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.610
AKA "Ygg."

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:03.260
This world's based off Akira's memories, 
but it's Yggdrasil that's bringing it to life.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.440
Oh, and Ygg was also the one 
who drew up Alma's design.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.440
Huh... So she's like Alma's mom, huh?

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:14.990
This is no time to be making a family tree. 
We need to get outta here.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:19.550
How about directly telling Akira 
that this is a fantasy world?

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.920
But it's one that he desired.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.170
He'll just refuse to accept it.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.740
He has to realize the truth himself.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:33.050
He might come to his senses if we do
something that didn't happen during his life.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.620
Like what?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.950
Well...

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:44.380
You okay, Minami?

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.700
I heard you've got a fever.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.460
I'm fine.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.920
Hey, what?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.680
Looking good!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.290
On to the next stage!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:06.810
S-Say, have you ever k-kissed anyone?

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:09.370
N-No.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.820
W-Wanna give it a shot, then?

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.360
B-But...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:18.340
I-I mean, this is all virtual,
anyway. Not real life.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.800
No!

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:32.280
Akira's mine! Keep your paws off him!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.260
Who's that?

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.790
Oh, you're that girl 
from the courtyard earlier.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:42.300
Snap!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.200
What did you do to Akira?

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.350
I just put him to sleep for a bit.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.060
Wake him up right now.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:57.160
Even if he realizes the truth, 
he has only a harsh reality waiting for him.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:03.210
If you truly want the best for him, 
let him stay here.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.660
Who are you, really?

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.230
I'm Ygg.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.740
His wife-to-be.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:16.920
Hang on.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.620
"Ygg"...? No way!

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.060
Anyway, I will protect his happiness!

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:31.020
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:34.480
W-We're out on the street?

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.710
What's going on?

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.060
L-Look!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.010
Y-Yo, help!

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.320
What's with that video-game monster?!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.320
Alma!

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:52.950
You saved my ass. Thanks.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.290
We're not out of the woods yet.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.710
What happened?

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:02.330
We're still investigating the cause,

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:08.650
but it seems they've been disconnected 
from Akira while trapped in VR.

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:13.390
Come on, Akira. This ain't funny, man.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.840
At least we made it to Akira's
place in one piece.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.450
Is the girl we met in the infirmary 
the one sending those monsters?

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:22.590
Probably.

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:23.770
Where's Minami?

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:29.130
He really was just an ordinary high schooler.

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.060
Yeah.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:33.580
<b>Meat 'n' potatoes, packed to the brim!</b>

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:33.580
<b>Special Stamina Fried Rice</b>

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.300
He sure loved to cook, huh?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.690
Is that an album?

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:41.200
He looks so funny!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:46.250
Shuichi, his big brother, 
must have taken these.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.680
How can you tell?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:52.560
His love for his little brother 
shines through in this photo.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.720
I had one myself.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:59.270
Akira really was a normal boy 
living in our world.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.210
Minami?

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:11.360
What that girl said hit home a bit.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:15.580
Akira might actually be happier 
staying in this world.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.630
But that's still not right! 
You gotta pick yourself up and move on!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.460
Akira has to, and so do we.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.180
Hello?

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.640
<i>Finally got through, yeesh.</i>

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.550
Kondo?!

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:36.000
<i>Listen up. The only way out for you guys 
is to make Akira face reality.</i>

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.710
What's happening to him?

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:40.970
<i>We can't disconnect him on our end.</i>

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.600
<i>Looks like he's in school over there.</i>

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:47.100
<i>But there's a program guarding him 
and keeping y'all away.</i>

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:50.160
How can we take out those monsters?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.300
Guns acquired!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.050
How did we end up having to raid 
a police station? We're cops!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.170
Right...

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.070
Found one.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:11.380
This will help us 
take at least a little control back.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.330
Everyone ready?

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:17.430
Let's go wake Akira up!

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:21.360
Was this really the best car we could use?

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.370
Remember, we're in Akira's fantasy.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.980
Be thankful we even found a car.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:28.410
The school's in sight!

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.620
So you've come.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:37.980
We'll handle things here.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.750
You go on ahead, Minami!

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:48.340
Roger that!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:53.480
Bring it! 
I'll show you that payback's a bitch!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.940
Those monsters are scary!

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:28.100
Y'know, even if I do get to Akira, 
can I really make him face reality?

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.760
You can do it.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:35.580
This world's been distorted by his will.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:39.890
If you can figure out what the biggest
inconsistency is, you can get through to him.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.130
Inconsistency?

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.830
Right!

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.030
I'm glad you realized.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.450
Take care of him for me.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.470
Was that...

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.500
Alisa, can you monitor things?

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:05.390
Aye.

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:07.100
<i>I want to try something.</i>

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:08.200
Go for it.

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:12.760
Yeah...

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.380
I really am forgetting something.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:18.400
But...

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.400
Akira.

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:23.660
Minami? Wait, how'd you get hurt?

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:31.180
You really are a totally
ordinary high schooler, huh?

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:34.280
Gee, sorry for being ordinary. 
It actually bothers me a little.

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:40.950
I wish we could've met 
under these circumstances instead.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:46.000
But hiding in a fantasy 
isn't going to solve anything.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:54.910
I realized that this world 
didn't have a single mirror.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.760
You didn't wanna see one.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.510
But you need to take a good look, Akira!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:10.140
Wait, you're...

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.440
Beta!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.560
Stop it!

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.390
Huh? Is this really my arm?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.240
What's going on?

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.060
What did I...

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.920
Snap out of it, Akira!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:42.970
You were a cheeky, pervy, ordinary high-schooler 
who hated tech and loved to cook!

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:48.540
Then you got in an accident, spent years
in a coma, and were reduced to a brain!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.620
And you are our squadmate. One of us.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:00.460
Oh... So that's my reality.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.240
I remember now. Thanks, Minami.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:22.400
What the...

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.790
Akira must've snapped out of it!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.160
Phew, took long enough.

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:32.040
Game over. Too bad.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.670
Everyone's come to!

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:40.330
Sheesh.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.180
Akira.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.220
Minami.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:57.800
Out, Yggdrasil. You did all that, didn't you?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.430
I'm sorry.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:06.860
But I couldn't help myself after seeing 
how well that boy syncs with machines!

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.220
Professor Iriya used to say the same thing.

00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:13.350
He seems to have remembered something crucial:

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.770
Beta's existence.

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:20.280
EX-ARM Number 11?

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:25.320
So, this "Beta" was the one 
behind the Tokyo Attack?

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:31.600
It's him.

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:34.980
Beta!

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:40.170
As long as you're around, 
this vicious cycle will never break.

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:44.280
If I can catch you 
and get all the answers I need,

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.980
I might be able to take back what I've lost.

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.340
I ain't no machine.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:53.160
I'm a human by the name of Natsume Akira!

00:23:26.160 --> 00:23:29.670
Looks like criminal scum from across the world 
are flocking to the EX-ARMs.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:33.050
I didn't expect that thing 
to be put up for sale, though.

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:36.360
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 006 - EX-ARM Auction."

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>EX-ARM Auction</b>

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:39.670
Retrieve all the EX-ARMs! 
This is an order!
